## 4. conclusion
  - st_dev/st_ino are identical across delete+recreate on this fs (ext4/f2fs), so (dev,ino) alone
    cannot prove 'the file was replaced' on Android.
  - shorter recreate still resets the offset via the 'size < offset => truncation' rule (safe).
  - recreate that is LONGER than the old offset is NOT detectable by (dev,ino): residual risk,
    reported as a follow-up item (would need e.g. ctime/i_version in the saved identity).
